OL,3,GNEWSAWW2 airman who fell 18,000ft
OL,4,Aremembered at museum
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn airman who is believed to have
OL,7,Fsurvived an 18,000ft (5,486m) fall from
OL,8,Fa burning plane without a parachute is
OL,9,Fbeing remembered with a new museum
OL,10,Fdisplay.
OL,12,FFlt Sgt Nicholas Alkemade was 21 years
OL,13,Fold when he was in a Lancaster bomber
OL,14,Fflying over Germany, in March 1944,
OL,15,Fwhen he fell to the woodland below.
OL,17,FMiraculously, he said fir trees and the
OL,18,Fdeep snow cushioned his fall.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,374,370,200,160,0,100
